            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_5eee1983829a0a9512ac9b20",
            "source_text": "Similarly,\nin LSTMs we have two dedicated gates for such purposes: the input gate $\\mathbf{I}_t$ governs how much we take new data into account via $\\tilde{\\mathbf{C}}_t$ and the forget gate $\\mathbf{F}_t$ addresses how much of the old memory cell content $\\mathbf{C}_{t-1} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times h}$ we retain.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b037",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "f87dae16c4798192b496b3fc0c93b3e30bc95a6ff23a95a4bd14cff3c0fa96e4",
            "context_id": "ctx_b2ecc4429423fc36a19369d3",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_82a449631f50a21335913618",
            "source_text": "```{.python .input}\ndef get_lstm_params(vocab_size, num_hiddens, device):\n    num_inputs = num_outputs = vocab_size\n\n    def normal(shape):\n        return np.random.normal(scale=0.01, size=shape, ctx=device)\n\n    def three():\n        return (normal((num_inputs, num_hiddens)),\n                normal((num_hiddens, num_hiddens)),\n                np.zeros(num_hiddens, ctx=device))\n\n    W_xi, W_hi, b_i = three()  # Input gate parameters\n    W_xf, W_hf, b_f = three()  # Forget gate parameters\n    W_xo, W_ho, b_o = three()  # Output gate parameters\n    W_xc, W_hc, b_c = three()  # Candidate memory cell parameters\n    # Output layer parameters\n    W_hq = normal((num_hiddens, num_outputs))\n    b_q = np.zeros(num_outputs, ctx=device)\n    # Attach gradients\n    params = [W_xi, W_hi, b_i, W_xf, W_hf, b_f, W_xo, W_ho, b_o, W_xc, W_hc,\n              b_c, W_hq, b_q]\n    for param in params:\n        param.attach_grad()\n    return params\n```",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b038",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "3a89755d01def81dfe93e85ab32c15756b167fd48c53ebe335576641d3674de9",
            "context_id": "ctx_d97ae77a3b700998ac63cadd",
            "evidence_roles": [
